Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.36,0:00:04.05,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,What... is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.58,0:00:08.37,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I feel as if my soul's been flung \Nsomewhere unimaginably far...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.27,0:00:17.25,italics,Leviathan,0,0,0,,Has it truly been a thousand \Nyears since we last assembled?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.75,0:00:21.15,italics,Behemoth,0,0,0,,We have not since the Silver Age.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.86,0:00:25.22,italics,Bahamut,0,0,0,,The one back then was \Nexceptional, as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.22,0:00:27.06,italics,Bahamut,0,0,0,,The one who, at level 255,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.06,0:00:31.55,italics,Bahamut,0,0,0,,tamed all four of us and \Nreturned our powers to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.80,0:00:33.15,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,How...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.15,0:00:36.56,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I've never heard these voices \Nbefore, but I know them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.98,0:00:40.25,italics,Leviathan,0,0,0,,The day will soon come
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.25,0:00:43.45,italics,Leviathan,0,0,0,,when we all come together and \Nfully regain our powers.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.45,0:00:46.06,italics,Leviathan,0,0,0,,It will be the most auspicious day \Nsince the moment of creation!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.25,0:00:51.25,Default,Humbaba,0,0,0,,My goodness. You seem \Nquite fond of this boy,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.25,0:00:54.06,Default,Humbaba,0,0,0,,"Mad Dog" Leviathan.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.53,0:01:04.49,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Was I... hearing things?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.89,0:01:06.62,Default,OnlookerA,0,0,0,,A voice from the heavens...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.83,0:01:09.49,Default,Onlookers,0,0,0,,That was God's voice, wasn't it?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.90,0:01:10.23,top,Onlookers,0,0,0,,I heard it, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.49,0:01:12.64,Default,Onlookers,0,0,0,,The heavens have placed their \Nhopes in the Thirteenth Prince!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.61,0:01:11.80,top,Onlookers,0,0,0,,Incredible!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.62,0:01:19.80,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,I heard it, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.80,0:01:22.88,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Impressive, boy.\NThis is a happy occasion!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.27,0:01:24.76,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,You, too, Prince Indra?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.19,0:01:26.23,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Gigi.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.23,0:01:27.56,Default,Gigi,0,0,0,,Y-Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.86,0:01:32.95,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Give five... no, ten rean to \Neveryone standing around here.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.95,0:01:35.27,top,Onlookers,0,0,0,,All hail the Wise Prince!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.20,0:01:34.58,Default,Gigi,0,0,0,,Yes, Master!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.14,0:01:36.91,Default,Onlookers,0,0,0,,Thank you!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.96,0:01:41.15,top,Onlookers,0,0,0,,Banzai! Banzai! Banzai!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.91,0:01:40.06,Default,Onlookers,0,0,0,,He is truly the one\Nacknowledged by the divine!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.04,0:01:43.83,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,On an auspicious day,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.77,0:01:44.18,top,Gigi,0,0,0,,Here you go!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.83,0:01:47.49,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,a time when something good happens,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.49,0:01:49.83,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,it is considered the duty\Nof the nobility to share it
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.83,0:01:52.23,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,with everyone rather than\Nkeep it all to themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.51,0:01:57.00,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,It is said that third-rate \Nnobles oppose this,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.66,0:02:00.96,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,second-rate nobles go along \Nwith it out of sheer pride,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.28,0:02:05.29,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,and first-rate nobles just do it as \Nif it's the natural course of action.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.51,0:02:11.83,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,If I may, Wise Prince...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.83,0:02:14.93,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,Please allow me to refuse \Nthis aid you have offered.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.73,0:02:16.85,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.43,0:02:20.09,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,Because I wish to become your knight.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.09,0:02:22.86,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,To do that, I must \Nadvance on my own merit
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.86,0:02:25.08,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,and become worthy of \Nliving in your service.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.79,0:02:27.87,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Denied.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.60,0:02:29.54,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.86,0:02:32.67,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,To accept help and then slack \Noff would be inexcusable,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.67,0:02:35.79,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,but only second-rate knights \Naccept out of sheer pride.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.13,0:02:37.50,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,S-Second-rate?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.50,0:02:41.61,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,If you want to be first-rate,\Ndo not be ashamed to accept aid.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.61,0:02:43.63,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Just give even more back to your master.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.54,0:02:48.76,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,If you want to be worthy of me, \Nthat's what you need to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.62,0:02:51.20,Default,Cheryl,0,0,0,,Understood!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.40,0:02:57.57,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Impressive. It only took \None well-spoken line.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.37,0:03:01.08,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,He's grown into one intriguing little sprout.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.42,0:03:03.04,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Brilliant, is he not?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.33,0:03:08.67,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,That is why I thought...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.04,0:03:15.33,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,your granddaughter would \Nbe perfect for him.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:36.50,0:03:38.50,sign_generic,Title,0,0,0,,{\fade(109,0)\c&H4F7C81&\bord0\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs10\pos(320,142.5)}Born Blessed, So I'll Obtain Ultimate Power
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.50,0:03:38.50,sign_generic,Title,0,0,0,,{\fade(109,0)\p1\bord2\c&H291505&\alpha&H255&\3c&H2986A5&\fscx87\pos(311,141.167)}m 0 0 l 235 0 l 225 8 l 235 15 l 18 15 l 30 8 l 18 0
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.75,0:04:56.76,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,We are outside the palace.\NNo need for excessive formalities.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.76,0:04:59.58,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Uncle, stand beside me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.58,0:05:00.61,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.69,0:05:11.34,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,And now, Leviathan.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.78,0:05:13.39,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Just slight menace.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.39,0:05:16.36,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Only enough to inspire awe and respect.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.36,0:05:19.34,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Good. I don't sense any treachery.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.34,0:05:21.04,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,So melodramatic.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.59,0:05:25.89,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,I'm surprised he can keep his \Ncool at such a young age.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.20,0:05:29.06,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,He's gotta be the number \None prince, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.06,0:05:32.11,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,That is why I called him the "Wise."
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.11,0:05:35.46,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,It's just as fitting as \Nyour "Lightning," no?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.08,0:05:40.85,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,I'll be just a thundering old \Nfart soon enough, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.85,0:05:43.20,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Noah will grow into his "Wise" title.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.20,0:05:47.81,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,It has been determined that he will make \Nhis first campaign alone, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.45,0:05:51.50,Default,OnlookerB,0,0,0,,A solo first campaign?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.50,0:05:54.68,Default,OnlookerC,0,0,0,,Don't they normally take a robust escort?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.68,0:05:57.20,Default,OnlookerD,0,0,0,,But with this one, I can believe it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.20,0:05:59.64,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,The people have turned \Ntheir attention to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.20,0:06:02.80,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,This would be an opportune \Ntime to escort His Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.43,0:06:05.12,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Wait, could it be...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.58,0:06:10.46,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I knew it. Then I'll \Ngladly accept his favor.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.46,0:06:13.07,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,This is what's so amazing about Noah.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.30,0:06:19.86,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I told you all that to create an \Nopportunity for him to escort me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.86,0:06:22.70,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,He understood that and leapt on board.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.36,0:06:25.85,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Oh? Impressive.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.85,0:06:28.27,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,I didn't even notice.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.27,0:06:32.27,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,As free-wheeling as you are, \Nyou lack sensitivity.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.27,0:06:35.88,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,That's why you and your wife quarrel \Nendlessly over trivial things.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.66,0:06:39.38,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,You got that right!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.38,0:06:42.91,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,All the more reason to feel at \Nease giving him my granddaughter!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.82,0:06:50.89,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Now, Uncle, we must talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.41,0:07:05.11,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,So, what'd you wanna talk about?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.06,0:07:07.31,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.66,0:07:10.78,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Luthier.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.55,0:07:26.16,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I think I will disinherit \Nthe crown prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.61,0:07:31.51,sign_generic,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\b1\fade(541,723)\c&H00070B&\pos(320, 205)}Episode 11
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.61,0:07:31.51,sign_generic,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\b1\fade(541,723)\c&H00070B&\pos(320, 225)}Disinheritance
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.59,0:07:41.40,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I had hoped things would work out,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.40,0:07:45.31,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,but I've been left with no \Nchoice but to deem him unfit.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.31,0:07:46.73,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.73,0:07:48.66,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,The matter with Gilbert.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.52,0:07:50.97,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.73,0:07:54.94,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I couldn't let His Majesty \Nkill his own child,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.94,0:07:59.00,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,so I tried to convince him to give \NGilbert no more than a life sentence.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.79,0:08:02.33,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,But then the crown prince...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.48,0:08:06.55,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,That in itself was not a mistake,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.55,0:08:09.97,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,but there must have been some \Nother way to go about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.97,0:08:12.31,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,That scared the hell outta me, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.86,0:08:17.10,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,If he were to become the emperor, \Nthere'd definitely be a major purge.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.34,0:08:18.47,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.47,0:08:22.98,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,In particular, Henry, Oscar, and Noah \Nwould be the first ones eliminated.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.98,0:08:25.94,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Such pettiness and cruelty...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.94,0:08:29.61,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I cannot allow such a man to succeed me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.04,0:08:32.34,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,That's fine, but what's next?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.34,0:08:35.01,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Who's gonna be the next crown prince?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.01,0:08:36.38,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I haven't decided.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.77,0:08:40.47,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,You can't be like that. \NYou're an old man now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.47,0:08:45.67,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,If you drop dead before you choose \Nan heir, it'll divide the nation.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.89,0:08:51.82,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,His Majesty must have \Ncome to Indra for advice
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.82,0:08:54.81,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,because no one else could \Nbe so frank with him.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.89,0:08:58.28,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,To say I haven't decided is inaccurate.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.59,0:09:03.03,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,But if I announce my decision now, \Nit would only lead to more feuding.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.03,0:09:06.68,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,That's still better than leaving \Nthe crown prince's post vacant.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.68,0:09:07.92,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,True.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.58,0:09:10.68,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,If I may speak, Your Majesty...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.68,0:09:11.60,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.08,0:09:16.56,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Perhaps you could tell the public only \Nthat you have prepared your will...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.60,0:09:21.92,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,and that the name of your \Nheir is written in it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.92,0:09:23.49,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,That won't work.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.49,0:09:27.07,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Anyone could forge a \Nwill after he's dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.07,0:09:32.33,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Yes, which is why His Majesty would \Nhide his will inside his body.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.89,0:09:37.80,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,A simple example would be a false \Ntooth with writing engraved in it,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.80,0:09:39.93,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,or perhaps some sort of magic...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.46,0:09:45.69,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,I get it. If it's on his person at \Nall times, no one can change it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.57,0:09:50.06,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Remarkable, Noah! That is a fine idea!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.33,0:09:59.21,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,You wait outside, as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.90,0:10:01.75,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Let no one enter.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.75,0:10:02.62,Default,Cruz,0,0,0,,Yes, sire.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.00,0:10:04.37,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Who's he?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.37,0:10:05.80,Default,Cruz,0,0,0,,Not to worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.29,0:10:09.70,Default,Cruz,0,0,0,,He is a liaison, the sort who is always \Npresent at occasions of this nature.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.70,0:10:13.63,Default,Cruz,0,0,0,,He cannot hear, speak, or read.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.38,0:10:18.37,Default,Cruz,0,0,0,,I will take my leave now.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.27,0:10:27.15,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Now, Noah, you've made \Nan excellent proposal.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.15,0:10:28.68,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I've decided to employ it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.68,0:10:31.20,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Yes, sire. Also, one other thing...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.20,0:10:34.31,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I think command of our full military \Nshould be returned to you,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.74,0:10:37.44,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,including Henry's post as \Nminister-prince of military affairs
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.44,0:10:39.82,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,and mine as governor-general \Nof the first imperial guard.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.07,0:10:45.84,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Good point. If anyone who objects to \Nhis will is in command of any forces,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.84,0:10:49.39,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,he could remove all the others \Nand install himself as emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.39,0:10:51.04,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,A sound argument...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.76,0:10:55.54,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,but I wouldn't have expected it from \None of the guys who'll lose his post.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.54,0:10:57.38,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Impressive, boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.38,0:10:59.96,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,He'll make a fine husband \Nfor your granddaughter, no?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.96,0:11:01.13,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,He sure will.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.81,0:11:09.45,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,An edict expressing gratitude to me while \Nrelieving me of my governor-general post.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.69,0:11:16.78,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,And that one will be for Henry.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.77,0:11:25.45,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,That was an awfully simplistic order.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.45,0:11:28.47,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I suppose he's been trained \Nso that he can only carry out
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.47,0:11:30.41,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,a certain few specific orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.41,0:11:33.91,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,So how are you gonna handle the \Ncrown prince's disinheritance?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.91,0:11:41.63,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,In my opinion as minister-prince \Nof justice,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.63,0:11:43.54,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,that's entirely up to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.12,0:11:50.71,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Your Majesty is free to name or \Ndisinherit your heir as you please.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.71,0:11:53.39,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,No one can meddle in your decision.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.86,0:11:55.31,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.31,0:12:02.11,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,But unlike Gilbert, Albert has not \Ncommitted a specific offense.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.11,0:12:06.65,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,For that reason, it may be best to \Nlet him remain a prince, at least.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.65,0:12:09.18,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Then how about this?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.18,0:12:12.37,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,"Albert has not committed treason \Nagainst me or the empire,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.37,0:12:14.93,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,but he is not capable enough for \Nme to entrust the empire to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.93,0:12:17.13,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,He will thus be stripped of\Nhis role as crown prince,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.13,0:12:18.42,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,but retain the title of prince."
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.79,0:12:20.62,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I think that sounds excellent.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.62,0:12:23.51,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Great. So, emperor,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.51,0:12:26.38,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,does Albert have any chance \Nof becoming your heir again?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.63,0:12:27.83,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.84,0:12:34.52,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,He really has given up on Albert.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.52,0:12:37.82,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Then you should probably make that clear.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.06,0:12:41.52,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Perhaps you could give him a title?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.52,0:12:44.65,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,One like "Ended Prince," for\Nexample, implying that he
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.65,0:12:46.11,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,cannot advance beyond "prince"?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.11,0:12:47.02,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Oh?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.50,0:12:49.89,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Yes, I like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.89,0:12:52.47,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Noah, thank you for your counsel.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.83,0:12:58.45,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Hmm... This won't do...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.45,0:13:02.44,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,What's the deal?\NThat's a lot of mistakes.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.44,0:13:05.38,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,And the writing's so convoluted, \Nno one'll understand it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.38,0:13:06.29,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,What's wrong with you?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.82,0:13:09.80,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I'm taking my son's inheritance away.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.80,0:13:12.90,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Even if this isn't as \Ngrave as taking his life,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.90,0:13:14.38,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I can hardly bear it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.75,0:13:18.59,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,I get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.59,0:13:22.45,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Just keep redoing it until you \Ncan write it without hesitation.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.87,0:13:25.95,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, if I may...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.21,0:13:30.49,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Perhaps you should leave what \Nyou've written exactly as it is?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.24,0:13:33.74,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It will remain on the record \Nas an official edict,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.07,0:13:38.04,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,so your feelings will be preserved \Nin a way that Albert can see them.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.72,0:13:40.34,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,And if he can accept that
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.34,0:13:44.49,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,and continue to push on as a \Nprince for the empire's sake...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.88,0:13:47.32,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,If only you had been...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.22,0:13:54.84,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I will do that. Excellent advice.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.12,0:13:56.85,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Thank you, Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.54,0:14:13.62,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Hold it!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.20,0:14:15.75,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,What is it, boy?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.75,0:14:19.04,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,This eunuch visibly reacted \Nafter looking at the edict.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.04,0:14:20.28,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.28,0:14:22.06,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,And then he hesitated.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.06,0:14:24.05,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Because he knows what it says.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.06,0:14:27.05,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,You won't escape!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.07,0:14:32.26,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Cruz!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.26,0:14:34.44,Default,Cruz,0,0,0,,I-Is something the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.31,0:14:37.98,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,That man can read.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.98,0:14:39.03,Default,Cruz,0,0,0,,Wha—
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.74,0:14:43.65,Default,Cruz,0,0,0,,This is a result of my own negligence!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.65,0:14:45.95,Default,Cruz,0,0,0,,Please... Please forgive me!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.95,0:14:47.99,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,How shall he be punished, Noah?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.99,0:14:51.64,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Execution. To be carried out immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.64,0:14:52.82,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,The reason?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.82,0:14:55.06,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,He lied about being unable to read
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.06,0:14:58.23,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,so he could assume what could be \Nconsidered a key role in the empire.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.23,0:15:01.08,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,He has sullied\NYour Majesty's imperial court.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.58,0:15:04.95,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,Shouldn't we get some information \Nout of him before we kill him?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.68,0:15:07.75,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,That would tell us who is behind this,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.75,0:15:10.22,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,making it possible to \Npunish them both, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.04,0:15:12.56,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,What if it was Albert?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.15,0:15:16.05,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Or one of the other princes?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.05,0:15:17.68,Default,Indra,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.68,0:15:21.67,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Yes. Let's not do that. \NThank you for your counsel.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.67,0:15:25.86,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Noah, please continue to serve me \Nas minister-prince of justice.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.65,0:15:27.86,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.86,0:15:29.87,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,What shall we do with Cruz?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.38,0:15:33.58,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,His only crime is a lack of oversight.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.98,0:15:36.23,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Six months of reduced pay should suffice.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.70,0:15:38.54,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,You heard him, Cruz.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.91,0:15:40.55,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,See to it, as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.55,0:15:42.51,Default,Cruz,0,0,0,,Y-Yes, Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.51,0:15:44.86,Default,Cruz,0,0,0,,Thank you so much!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.94,0:15:54.22,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Is it done?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.54,0:15:56.77,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,Since the man was a eunuch,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.77,0:15:59.60,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,I carried out his punishment personally.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.60,0:16:01.21,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,And?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.21,0:16:03.41,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,Prince Noah is remarkable.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.41,0:16:07.58,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,I almost wonder if he can read minds.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.00,0:16:09.42,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Albert...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.06,0:16:11.58,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,What will you do?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.58,0:16:14.85,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I... know not.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.21,0:16:18.88,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Whoever he may be,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.88,0:16:23.04,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,even if I can't entrust the empire \Nto him, he is still my son.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.21,0:16:30.84,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Incidentally, are you familiar \Nwith the name "Leviathan"?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.84,0:16:33.17,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,Yes. He was one of the four sages
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.17,0:16:37.42,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,who lent their powers to the \Nemperor during the Silver Age.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.42,0:16:42.22,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,It seems that Leviathan is \Nlending his powers to Noah now.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.45,0:16:44.17,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,Well, that is splendid!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.17,0:16:48.52,Default,Noizhill,0,0,0,,If anyone can surpass the Silver Age,\Nperhaps it is Prince Noah!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.52,0:16:51.98,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Yes. He does have the \Npotential, at least.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.50,0:16:55.19,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I will watch carefully
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.19,0:16:57.98,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,to see how he grows from here.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.62,0:17:02.25,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,At your leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.92,0:17:11.26,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,Um... Your Highness?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.26,0:17:13.95,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,Where are you heading from here?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.95,0:17:18.70,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It's unusual for you to insert \Nyourself in conversations like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.70,0:17:21.01,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,I-I'm very sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.01,0:17:23.29,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,It's just that you looked \Nso lost in thought...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.29,0:17:26.18,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It's fine. Your assessment is correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.18,0:17:27.01,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,Then...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.00,0:17:29.16,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Remain at ease.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.64,0:17:33.31,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,We are indeed riding into a challenge, \Nbut our lives are not in danger.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.31,0:17:34.36,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.77,0:17:37.86,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,We're headed to my brother's,\Nthe crown prince's, mansion.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.97,0:17:59.83,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,High above in the clear blue sky
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.83,0:18:03.74,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,The white birds are taking flight
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.74,0:18:08.60,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,Signaling that a new wind has arrived
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.51,0:18:09.43,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,Well, this is truly a rare visit.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.60,0:18:11.50,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,Singing to the town below
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.01,0:18:13.91,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,I wasn't expecting the minister-prince \Nof justice at the peak of his popularity.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.50,0:18:13.64,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,In the heat of the busy city street
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.64,0:18:15.73,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,And the roaring voices of the crowd
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.41,0:18:17.44,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I have come for an audience with \NYour Highness the Crown Prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.73,0:18:17.44,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,Everything that we have \Nwaited for is here
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.44,0:18:23.68,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,The door to a new age opens wide
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.44,0:18:19.90,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Please forgive me for \Nvisiting without notice.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.90,0:18:22.51,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,You're always so formal.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.51,0:18:25.84,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,Well, I suppose that's why you're \Nthe minister-prince of justice.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.68,0:18:26.41,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,Holding on to just a single wish inside
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.84,0:18:29.78,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,Anyway, relax.\NHere, we're just two brothers.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.41,0:18:29.78,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,Counting all the freezing \Nnights I have survived
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.78,0:18:31.63,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.28,0:18:34.48,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Stand by outside the mansion.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.48,0:18:35.47,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.82,0:18:40.22,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Having my guard wait outside is a show \Nof my trust in the crown prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.79,0:18:43.07,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I'm sure Shirley understands that now.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.43,0:18:46.01,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,Would you prefer the\Nliving room or the garden?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.01,0:18:50.10,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I've heard that your garden is kept \Nby the renowned gardener, Torrant.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.48,0:18:52.98,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I've been hoping for a chance to see it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.98,0:18:55.95,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,Oh, yes, I never showed it to you, did I?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.95,0:18:58.12,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,Very good. Right this way, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.27,0:19:01.23,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It's beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.23,0:19:02.59,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,You can tell?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.21,0:19:06.23,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Yes. That tree with the \Ndouble trunks, for example.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.23,0:19:08.63,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I've never seen one so magnificent.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.63,0:19:10.74,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,Your eyes are as keen as ever.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.74,0:19:13.84,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,That was a gift from a member of my \Nhousehold that I sent away to work.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.84,0:19:15.95,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,It cost 50,000 rean, apparently.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.95,0:19:18.06,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I can believe that.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.06,0:19:20.66,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,I'll have it sent to your mansion later.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.29,0:19:24.71,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,You saw its quality with one look.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.71,0:19:28.22,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,The tree itself would be happier \Nwith a man who understands it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.22,0:19:30.90,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Then I will gratefully accept it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.90,0:19:34.80,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,This will be the second time I've \Npersonally given you something.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.80,0:19:38.27,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,You seem to have mastered \Nthat magic sword, no?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.57,0:19:41.19,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,I only gave it to you as a little joke,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.19,0:19:43.28,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,but that has taught me
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.28,0:19:47.88,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,that great power only belongs in \Nthe hands of the right people.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.38,0:19:56.12,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Summer is upon us again.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.39,0:19:57.89,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,Hm? Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.32,0:20:00.46,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I asked earlier,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.78,0:20:03.96,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,and His Majesty said he will travel north \Nto escape the heat again this year.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.96,0:20:05.69,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,What differs from previous years
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.38,0:20:08.77,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,is that he intends to take \Nyou with him this year.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.31,0:20:11.23,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,In recent years,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.63,0:20:14.83,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,when the emperor left the \Ncapital to escape the heat,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.83,0:20:17.45,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,he had the crown prince \Nrule in his stead.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.79,0:20:22.68,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,This allowed him to gradually give the \Ncrown prince more government duties
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.68,0:20:25.90,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,as a rehearsal for his \Nfuture reign as emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.37,0:20:28.95,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,But doing away with that means...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.95,0:20:30.06,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,How much...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.88,0:20:32.65,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,do you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.22,0:20:36.35,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,His Majesty only gave me \Na roundabout explanation.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.35,0:20:42.17,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,He said he wanted to give you a thorough \Neducation on the essence of ruling.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.17,0:20:43.29,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,I beg your pardon?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.63,0:20:46.31,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,He is the kind of great ruler \Nwe see only once a millennia.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.84,0:20:51.93,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I imagine he has come up with many \Nmethods that we could never even imagine.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.60,0:20:55.98,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I can only guess that he wants \Nto teach them to you now.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.37,0:21:00.44,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,His Majesty does intend \Nto take Albert with him,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.44,0:21:04.37,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,but probably only because keeping him \Nclose means one less thing to worry about.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.87,0:21:07.24,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Even so,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.24,0:21:08.91,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,if spending time together
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.91,0:21:12.19,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,helps my brother understand\NHis Majesty's feelings...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.32,0:21:16.36,Default,Albert,0,0,0,,I see. Thank you, Noah.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.48,0:21:32.57,Default,Alichey,0,0,0,,Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.57,0:21:33.59,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Alichey.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.02,0:21:36.57,Default,Alichey,0,0,0,,I'm up next, so I came to greet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.57,0:21:37.43,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.96,0:21:41.10,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.43,0:21:44.67,Default,Alichey,0,0,0,,Nothing. I will sing \Nwith all I have in me,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.67,0:21:47.07,Default,Alichey,0,0,0,,just like you told me to.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.73,0:21:48.53,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.24,0:22:00.85,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,Sweetly echoing my mother's lullaby
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.85,0:22:06.21,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,Orange fire casting shadows on the wall
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.67,0:22:11.51,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,Feigning sleep I held on \Ntight to father's back
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.37,0:22:15.70,sign_generic,Credits,0,0,0,,{\an3\fade(443,366)\fnTimes New Roman\b1\c&HC4C4C4&\3c&H1E1E1F&\blur2\bord0.5\fs10\pos(114.667,221.334)}Translation:\NTiming:\NEditing:\NQuality Control:
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.37,0:22:15.70,sign_generic,Credits,0,0,0,,{\an1\fade(443,366)\fnTimes New Roman\b1\c&HC4C4C4&\3c&H1E1E1F&\blur2\bord0.5\fs10\pos(127,221.334)}Becky Cottrill\NEdgar Cruz\NGabriella Alabanza\NS Bilyeu
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.51,0:22:15.54,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,Safe in his arms
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.54,0:22:19.34,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,You must be strong
Dialogue: 0,0:22:19.34,0:22:24.42,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,To protect the weak
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.42,0:22:26.37,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,I know this truth well
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.37,0:22:32.09,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,Because he taught me so
Dialogue: 0,0:22:32.09,0:22:36.03,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,Crying in frustration
Dialogue: 0,0:22:36.03,0:22:39.77,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,My tears become a river now
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.77,0:22:49.21,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,Carrying hope to tomorrow
Dialogue: 0,0:22:44.25,0:22:45.27,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Enter.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.78,0:22:47.19,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Pardon me, Master.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:49.52,0:22:52.13,top,Zoey,0,0,0,,I'm sorry to visit so late at night.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:52.60,0:22:56.52,top,Zoey,0,0,0,,There is a woman here \Nwho wishes to see you.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:57.47,0:22:58.51,top,Noah,0,0,0,,Her name?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.51,0:23:00.37,top,Zoey,0,0,0,,Olivia Coil.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.93,0:23:02.73,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I don't know that name.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.73,0:23:07.10,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,But if she wasn't someone important, \NZoey would have sent her away.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.60,0:23:08.90,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Fine. Let her in.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:10.19,0:23:12.01,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,You said your name is Olivia?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:12.69,0:23:21.28,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,There is nothing we can \Ntake when we depart
Dialogue: 0,0:23:13.01,0:23:15.15,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,What is your business\Nhere at this hour?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.15,0:23:16.88,Default,Olivia,0,0,0,,I bring you a tip.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.43,0:23:20.88,Default,Olivia,0,0,0,,The crown prince, Second Prince Albert,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.28,0:23:25.05,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,Blooming in the glory
Dialogue: 0,0:23:22.69,0:23:24.79,Default,Olivia,0,0,0,,plans to lead\Na coup tonight...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.05,0:23:30.26,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,For the future I had always dreamed of
Dialogue: 0,0:23:30.26,0:23:32.24,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,I will stand right here
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.38,0:23:34.02,Default,Olivia,0,0,0,,and force His Majesty \Nto abdicate the throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.24,0:23:38.17,italicstop,Alichey,0,0,0,,Singing out a song of blessing
